WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:02.868
-I want to ask about something.

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.200
Right around Christmas,

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.534
we do this thing called
"Day Drinking" on the show.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.100
And I was doing it with Lizzo,
and your name came up.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.400
-I saw it.
-Yeah.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.534
And again, it must have been
very exciting,

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:12.567
because Lizzo, let me tell you,

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:13.868
one of the most charming
human beings.

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:14.934
I don't know if you've been
lucky enough to meet her.

00:00:14.934 --> 00:00:16.234
-I've never met her.
I watched --

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:17.534
I mean, I watched.
It was on the show.

00:00:17.534 --> 00:00:20.267
And when I heard Lizzo
say my name, I was like...

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:22.367
I got all excited.

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:23.934
By the way, it's a weird thing

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:26.834
when you're not expecting
to hear that and you hear it.

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:29.434
And that segment was hilarious,
by the way.

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:31.501
That whole -- Every time
you do it, it's so funny.

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:33.567
-She really did
sort of raise the bar.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:36.634
I keep telling people
she's so deeply funny.

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:38.367
Even while, like, inebriated,

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:40.767
she, like, talks like
a comedy writer.

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:43.501
-So funny, so charming.

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:45.467
Yeah, it was great.

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:48.367
-She also -- I've told this a
few times, but the great thing,

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:50.267
to bring it back to my dad,
you know,

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:52.300
one of her catchphrases
is "Bye, bitch."

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.334
-Right.
-And we left a message --

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:56.667
we left a voicemail for my dad,
and she said --

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:58.000
she ended it by saying,
"Bye, bitch."

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.267
-Yeah.

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:02.567
-Then independent of me,
she got my dad's information

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:05.267
and sent him flowers
with a note that said,

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:07.367
"I'm sorry
I called you a bitch."

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:11.033
And my brother and I
call him a bitch all the time.

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:12.968
We've never apologized.

00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:14.234
-You owe him a lot of flowers.

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:15.834
-Yeah, we owe him
a lot of flowers.

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:18.400
"You made us root for
the Steelers, you bitch."

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.367
So, anyway, but the reason
your name came up

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:25.434
is one of our writers walked
out, and he was wearing a mask,

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:27.934
and Lizzo -- and again,
she'd had a few drinks.

00:01:27.934 --> 00:01:32.067
She thought it was Paul Rudd.
She thought it was you.

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:33.334
So the writer's here today,

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:35.534
but first I want to show
the first half of the clip,

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:37.868
and then we're gonna bring out
the writer, Seth Reiss.

00:01:37.868 --> 00:01:41.400
So here's Lizzo noticing
our writer the first time.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.868
-Ohh, I'm calm now.

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:44.434
-Alright, let's bring him over.

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:46.501
-Paul [bleep] Rudd!

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:47.801
Paul Rudd!

00:01:47.801 --> 00:01:49.601
-Hey, Lizzo,
I know the real reason

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:50.868
you're breaking up with me

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:53.267
is that you met famous
Hollywood actor Paul Rudd,

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:55.033
who's now gonna
take his mask off,

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:57.000
and I want you to react to it
in real time.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.300
-[Bleep]

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:01.100
-Alright, so now we're gonna
bring out the writer.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.167
And we're gonna let you guys
decide, was Lizzo crazy?

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:08.901
[ Laughter, cheering ]

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:11.734
Alright, you know what?

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:14.968
Not -- Not --

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.200
Not as bad as I thought.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.234
I owe an apology to Lizzo.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:22.200
But now this is
the really exciting part, guys.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.901
'Cause again, I think
you're agreeing with Lizzo.

00:02:24.901 --> 00:02:26.701
This is not too far afield,

00:02:26.701 --> 00:02:28.834
until you see the rest
of the face.

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:30.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.701
A lot of other stuff can happen.

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:40.467
-This better not be --
This better --

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:41.868
Oh [bleep]

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:43.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:48.000
-I didn't even look.

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:54.400
-I need a tissue.
I need a tissue, please.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.801
No, here's the thing.

00:02:56.801 --> 00:03:00.767
You don't look anything
like [bleep] Paul Rudd.

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:01.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:03.801
-There we go.
Let's see both faces.

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:05.300
There we go.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:08.801
Paul and Seth Reiss,
brothers from another mother.

00:03:08.801 --> 00:03:10.634
-Thank you so much.
-It's like looking in a mirror.

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:12.667
-Thank you so much.
-It's like looking in a mirror!

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:16.033
-Thank you so much.
-And look at these two.

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:17.467
Two snowflakes can be alike.

00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:20.200
We'll be right back with more
from Paul Rudd, everybody.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

